          %div
            %h3#ObservationOfAnyonsInFQH Observation of anyons in fractional quantum Hall systems
            %p
              While the occurrence of
              = succeed "-excitations" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyon"} anyon
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+effect"} fractional quantum Hall effect
              is a robust theoretical prediction (see the references
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#AnyonsInTheQuantumHallEffectReferences"} above
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            %p An early claim of the observation of non-abelian anyons seems to remain unconfirmed:
            %ul
              %li
                Sanghun An, P. Jiang, H. Choi, W. Kang, S. H. Simon, L. N. Pfeiffer, K. W. West, K. W. Baldwin,
                %em Braiding of Abelian and Non-Abelian Anyons in the Fractional Quantum Hall Effect
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.3400"}> arXiv:1112.3400
                ]
            %p but, more recently, independent groups report consistent results across different materials:
            %p
              Observation in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gallium+arsenide"} gallium arsenide
              (
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
